# Local-service lifecycle

- Leave the ordinary local Next.js server and Supabase running for manual testing at handoff.
- Never stop a service merely because the task finished.
- Preserve services the user already had running.
- Clean up temporary test servers started by this task, including separate Playwright servers.
- Do not kill unrelated processes or use broad Node/Docker termination commands.
- If a restart is necessary, explain it, restart only the relevant service, and restore the ordinary development setup afterward where possible.
- Do not reset or reseed a user’s existing local database without explicit permission for that destructive operation.
- If clean-reset verification is needed, use an existing approved isolated test stack; otherwise pause for permission before resetting the shared stack.
- Report running services, app URLs, and any startup blocker at handoff.
- CI still cleans up its own services.
